[00:00.00]Hello, everyone. Today, we're going to talk about morning exercises.|大家好。今天我们要聊的是晨练。
[00:04.52]Morning exercises are a great way to start your day, right?|晨练是开启一天的好方式，对吧？
[00:07.86]Let me tell you about my morning routine.|我来跟你说说我的早晨日常。
[00:10.36]Every morning, I wake up at 6 a.m.|每天早上我六点起床。
[00:13.08]The first thing I do is stretch my arms and legs.|我做的第一件事就是伸展胳膊和腿。
[00:16.60]It feels really good after a night of sleep.|睡了一夜之后，这样特别舒服。
[00:19.34]Then, I put on my sports clothes and go for a run in the park near my house.|然后我换上运动服，去家附近的公园跑步。
[00:24.12]Running helps me feel fresh and ready for the day.|跑步让我神清气爽，准备好迎接新的一天。
[00:27.20]Sometimes I see people doing yoga or lifting weights.|有时我会看到有人在练瑜伽或举重。
[00:30.84]It's nice to see so many people taking care of their health.|看到这么多人在照顾自己的健康，真好。
[00:34.38]After my run, I drink a glass of water and have a light breakfast.|跑完步，我喝一杯水，吃一顿清淡的早餐。
[00:38.80]My favorite breakfast is toast with some vegetables.|我最喜欢的早餐是吐司配一些蔬菜。
[00:42.18]It's simple but healthy.|简单但健康。
[00:43.92]Did you know that exercising in the morning can actually make you more energetic throughout the day?|你知道吗？早上锻炼其实能让你一整天都更有精力。
[00:48.94]It's true.|这是真的。
[00:50.30]But I have to admit, sometimes I feel lazy and want to stay in bed.|但我得承认，有时候我也会犯懒，想赖在床上。
[00:54.68]That's why I set a goal for myself to exercise every morning.|所以我才给自己定了个目标：每天早上都锻炼。
[00:58.60]Having a goal helps me stay motivated.|有目标能让我保持动力。
[01:01.28]Speaking of goals, have you ever tried setting a daily exercise plan?|说到目标，你有没有试过制定每日运动计划？
[01:05.66]It's a great idea.|这是个好主意。
[01:07.18]You can start with something simple, like walking for 20 minutes or doing a few push-ups.|可以从简单的事开始，比如走 20 分钟，或者做几个俯卧撑。
[01:12.48]Remember, every little bit counts.|记住，每一点努力都算数。
[01:14.86]Now, let me tell you a funny story.|现在，我给你讲个有趣的事。
[01:16.84]One day, I saw a man in the park wearing his pajamas while jogging.|有一天，我在公园看到一个人穿着睡衣慢跑。
[01:20.84]I couldn't help but blush because it was so embarrassing.|我忍不住脸红，因为实在太尴尬了。
[01:24.88]But hey, at least he was exercising, right?|不过嘿，至少他在运动，对吧？
[01:27.86]Morning exercises don't have to be boring.|晨练不一定要枯燥。
[01:30.56]You can listen to music or podcasts while you work out.|锻炼时可以听音乐或播客。
[01:33.94]It makes the time go by faster.|这样时间过得快一些。
[01:36.18]Some people even exercise with their pets.|有些人甚至和宠物一起锻炼。
[01:39.04]I've seen dogs running alongside their owners in the park.|我在公园见过狗狗陪着主人一起跑。
[01:42.52]It's such a sweet sight.|那画面真温馨。
[01:44.30]If you're feeling stressed, morning exercises can help you relax.|如果你感到压力大，晨练能帮你放松。
[01:47.86]It's a great way to clear your mind before starting your day.|这是开始一天之前清空思绪的好方法。
[01:52.32]So if you don't have a morning exercise routine yet, why not give it a try?|所以如果你还没有晨练习惯，何不试一试呢？
[01:57.32]You might be surprised at how good it makes you feel.|你可能会惊讶于它带给你的感觉有多好。
[02:00.48]And remember, it's important to stay consistent.|还有，记住坚持很重要。
[02:03.68]Don't let a rainy day stop you from exercising.|别让下雨天阻止你锻炼。
[02:06.52]You can always do some indoor exercises like jumping jacks or stretching.|你随时可以做些室内运动，比如开合跳或拉伸。
